      "message": "@michaelludwig@google.com\n\nAn alternative to this patch is simply to call:\n```\n    void* fData \u003d nullptr;\n```\nin the destructor.\n\nAfter the MiraclePtr rewrite, `fData` is detected as dangling, because it points to storage. The storage is manually deleted first, which leave the pointer momentarilly dangling.\n\n---\n\nI decided to modernize it with unique_ptr and rely on the default destructor instead. Since pointer depends on storage, it is declared second, but destroyed in the reverse order, which makes the defaulted destructor valid.",
